The grammars in bundles/ (lib/bundles in the plugin) come from other projects and keep their licenses:

- adoc, bazel, bicep, cmake, erlang, hcl, jsp, kconfig, kotlin, mdx, terraform, twig and viml are under the license
  file in their own folder. hcl and terraform are HashiCorp's (IBM Corp.) HCL and Terraform grammars
  (https://github.com/hashicorp/syntax) under the Mozilla Public License 2.0; the files in their folders are their
  source form.
- The others are the grammars of the built-in extensions of Visual Studio Code
  (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/tree/main/extensions), under the license below. The grammars VS Code takes
  from other projects (each JSON file names its origin) keep those projects' licenses, listed in VS Code's
  ThirdPartyNotices.txt (https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/main/ThirdPartyNotices.txt). For the grammars
  this plugin ships, that license is also in the grammar's folder: LICENSE in bat, css, diff, docker (with NOTICE),
  dotenv, git-base, ini, javascript, less, log, make, powershell, scss, sql and typescript-basics.

